# Changelog

Update [`CHANGELOG.md`](../../CHANGELOG.md) whenever a feature or bugfix is ready for `main` (PR, merge, or a commit meant to land there). Do not wait to be asked.

## Format

Newest entries at the **top**, directly under the intro. Date is `YYYY-MM-DD`. Title is the feature or bug name.

```markdown
## YYYY-MM-DD — Short feature or bug title

- User-visible or notable change
- Another concrete bullet
```

## Rules

- Prepend. Never append to the bottom. Never rewrite older entries.
- One heading per feature or fix. Same-day items stay separate; the newest still goes first.
- Bullets are short and concrete (what changed / how it behaves). No PR numbers, file dumps, or commit hashes.
- Skip chore-only work (rules, comments, lockfile noise) unless the human asks.
- If several small fixes ship together as one change, use one title and several bullets.
